{"step_index":1041,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-25T13:36:10Z","input_tokens":2369,"cache_read_tokens":220501,"output_tokens":2347,"content":"### Phase 1 Implementation Complete: Interface Fix & Beginner-Focused Redesign\n\nAll objectives for **Phase 1 — Fix the interface** have been implemented and verified. The visualizer now feels like an intuitive, personal coding tutor rather than an overwhelming debugging dashboard.\n\n---\n\n### Key Improvements Made\n\n#### 1. Teaching Area is Now the Main Focus\n- **Proportional Space Allocation**: Updated the 3-column workspace grid in [styles.css](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/styles.css#L320-L333) from a cramped distribution to `minmax(270px, 310px) minmax(460px, 1.6fr) minmax(280px, 320px)`. The center teaching card now receives the primary visual focus (over 50% of the horizontal screen space).\n- **Readability & Typography**:\n  - Step title font increased to `21px` bold with clear tracking.\n  - Explanation body text (`.teach-meaning-text`) upgraded to `16.5px` with a generous `1.7` line-height for comfortable reading.\n  - Section labels now feature welcoming visual cues:\n    - `💡 What is happening?`\n    - `🎯 Why is this necessary?`\n    - `📦 Variable values now:`\n    - `➡️ What happens next?`\n  - Code highlight box styled with clean syntax coloring on a soft background with a prominent blue left accent bar.\n\n#### 2. Fixed Raw HTML Appearing in Explanations\n- **Root Cause Identified**: \n  1. In [app.js](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/app.js#L880-L895), `symbolsMeaning` was previously concatenated with inline `<span style=\"...\">` tags and passed through `formatMarkdown()`.\n  2. `formatMarkdown()` was converting all `<` and `>` characters into `&lt;` and `&gt;`, causing raw HTML tags like `<span style=\"font-size:13.5px; ...\">` to be literally printed on screen as text (as seen in your screenshot).\n- **Resolution**:\n  - Created a dedicated DOM element `<div id=\"teachSymbolsBox\" class=\"teach-symbols-callout hidden\"></div>` in [index.html](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/\n<truncated 2261 bytes>\node-flow-visualizer/app_build/index.html) | Hidden `#thonnyExprBox` and `#allIterationsSection` by default; updated button label to `📋 Execution History`; added `#teachSymbolsBox`. |\n| [app_build/app.js](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/app.js) | Set `showIterationsPanel = false` and `allGroupsCollapsed = true`; bound `#teachSymbolsBox`; fixed `formatMarkdown()` tag escaping; synchronized Advanced View toggle. |\n| [app_build/styles.css](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/styles.css) | Allocated `1.6fr` to the teaching area; improved typography and spacing; styled `.teach-symbols-callout`; added mobile column ordering. |\n| [app_build/explainer.js](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/explainer.js) | Verified deterministic rules and substep generation. |\n\n---\n\n### Verification & Testing Results\n\n- **Syntax Verification**: `node -c app_build/engine.js && node -c app_build/explainer.js && node -c app_build/app.js` passed with zero errors.\n- **Automated Trace & Max-Subarray Test**:\n  - `nums = [-2, 1, -3, 4, -1, 2, 1, -5, 4]` $\\rightarrow$ Result: **`6`** (50 steps) ✓\n  - `nums = [-5, -2, -8, -1, -4]` $\\rightarrow$ Result: **`-1`** (35 steps) ✓\n  - `nums = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]` $\\rightarrow$ Result: **`15`** (32 steps) ✓\n  - `nums = [-7]` $\\rightarrow$ Result: **`-7`** (13 steps) ✓\n  - `nums = [42]` $\\rightarrow$ Result: **`42`** (12 steps) ✓\n- **Raw HTML Check**: Zero unescaped HTML strings detected across all 50 steps.\n- **Navigation Verification**: `Previous Step` and `Next Step` accurately restore snapshots, variable states, and active line indicators without mutation leakage.\n- **Offline Integrity**: 100% deterministic local execution confirmed; no external APIs or network calls.\n\n---\n\n### Ready for Next Steps\nPhase 1 is complete. We can proceed to **Phase 2 — Improve teaching** (refining granular micro-explanations for operators and control flow) whenever you are ready.","thinking":"The core layout focuses on a prominent teaching area. Confirmed the main column receives 1.6fr flex prominence, with large readable text and good contrast for clear visual emphasis. Confirmed that the changes were strictly limited to specified files, preserving the engine and all constraints.\n\n\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
